Thread ; A thread is a lightweight process, it executes the small code of instrcutions.

Process : A process is a execution of a program.
-  its heavy weight.
- It has its own memory space, code, data and system resources.


Multithreading : It is a process of executing multiple threads simultaneously.
- It allows a program to perform multiple tasks at the same time.

Concurrency : It is the process of executing multiple process simultaneously.
- It allows multiple processes to run at the same time, but they may not be executing at the same time.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thread Methods  :
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. t1.start() -> Starts the thread and calls the run() method.

2. run() -> Actually execution of thread, it contains the actual that has to be executed by the thread.

3. t1.sleep() -> It is used to pause the execution of the thread for a specified amount of time.
- Suspends the current execution of the thread for a specified amount of time.

4. t1.Join() -> It stops the execution of the current thread until the thread on which join() is called is finished.
Main thread will wait until the thread t1 is finished, then it will continue its execution.

5. SetPriority -> It is used to set the priority of the thread.
Priorities -> Thread.MIN_PRIORITY (1) -> Lowest priority
              Thread.NORM_PRIORITY (5) -> Normal priority
              Thread.MAX_PRIORITY (10) -> Highest priority
- It is not mandatory to run based on priority, it is just a hint to the thread scheduler.

6. t1.interrupt()  -> It is used ti interrupt the current thread, that is in waiting or sleeping state.
- It immediate stops the execution of the thread and throws InterruptedException.

7. t1.yield()  -> It is a hint that current thread wants to allow other threads to execute.
- It is used to pause the current thread and allow other threads to execute.
- It is not guaranteed that the current thread will pause, it is just a hint to the thread scheduler.

8. t1.setDemon(Boolean true or false) -> It is used to set the thread as a daemon thread.
- A daemon thread is a thread that runs in the background and does not prevent the JVM from exiting when the program finishes.
- If a thread is set as a daemon thread, it will automatically terminate when all non-daemon threads have finished executing.

