Synchonization : It is a process of controlling the access of multiple threads to a shared resource.
- It is used to prevent the thread interference and consistency problem.
- It is achieved by using the synchronized keyword in Java.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Locks : It is a mechanism to control the access of multiple threads to a shared resource.
- It is used to prevent the thread interference and consistency problem.
- It is achieved by using the synchronized keyword in Java.
- It is also achieved by using the Lock interface in Java.

Two Types of Locks :
1. Intrinsic Locks (Synchronized Blocks) : It is a lock that is associated with
every object in Java. We cant see them but they are there.
- It is achieved by using the synchronized keyword in Java.
- These are automatic locks.

2. Explicit Locks (Lock Interface) : It is more advanced locks.
- These locks can be controlled by Lock interface in Java.
- It can be explicitly controlled by programmer, i.e when to LOCK and UNLOCK
- It provides more features than intrinsic locks, such as fairness, tryLock(), etc.

